      <memberdef kind="typedef" id="key__list_8h_1a5922b3fbf0411d276a899fcb01fb5e69" prot="public" static="no">
        <type>const char *(*</type>
        <definition>typedef const char*(* key_list_allocator_t) (struct tuple *tuple, const char *key, uint32_t key_sz)</definition>
        <argsstring>)(struct tuple *tuple, const char *key, uint32_t key_sz)</argsstring>
        <name>key_list_allocator_t</name>
        <briefdescription>
<para>We iterate over a functional index key list in two cases: when adding a new tuple or removing the old one. </para>        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>When adding a new tuple we need to copy functional index data to tuple memory, so provide an allocator for that. When removing an old index, it&apos;s fine to use a temporary memory area for the functional index key, since the key is only used to lookup the old tuple in the b+* tree, so we pass in a dummy allocator. </para>        </detaileddescription>
        <inbodydescription>
        </inbodydescription>
